Good video performance doesn't require any 3D drivers, only support
for the video overlay.  You'll still have some problems with the CPU
speed.  My SX164 at 533MHz is barely fast enough to play DVDs.  The
video drivers in XFree86 are too slow too, you'll have to use the more
efficient Vidix drivers.  These support using DMA to transfer the
video frames with some cards, which gives a considerable speed boost.

