If it's built from source, it should configure it properly.  Detect that I
have a Sable (or whatnot) and build a kernel that will work on that box if
generic won't work (which it won't in SMP mode on Sable).  Binary kernels
obviously need more attention, but even there Red Hat-based dists include a
few options, including, on i386 systems, kernels for i386 (older dists),
i586, i686, and some versions athlon.  You have an SMP capable kernel, and
on the enterprise lines a hugemem kernel.
 
> What I like about Gentoo is the system with USE flags, so I can
