I did a little testing using OPENSSL and there are some differences in
performance with CCC being the clear winner. The only hitch is, you can only
build static libs using CCC, shared libs are only supported under GCC. So
the speed doesn't do me any good in that regard since a LOT of programs out
there are looking for /usr/lib/libssl.so.0.9.7. :-(

