John Beardmore <wookie@wookie.demon.co.uk> writes:

> How do you force it to boot from a serial port ?  Does that require 
> anything special in the kernel ?

In "Character devices", you have to have "Standard/generic serial support"
and "Support for console on serial port" selected.  When booting, the
machine will automatically use the serial console if you don't have a
display adapter in the machine.  If you do, but you want to use serial
console anyway, you have to pass the "console=ttySN" option to the
kernel (where N is the serial port number, beginning with 0 for the
first serial port).  See the help for the "Support for console on
serial port" option.

