It should be impossible to plug a PCI card into an incompatible bus.
Take a look at your PCI cards.  Some have one notch in the connector,
some have two.  3V-only busses will only accept cards with two
notches.  All cards will work in 5V busses, since even 3V cards will
tolerate 5V signals.

>> One problem that can occur is if some PCI card requires its BIOS to
>> be run in order to initialize.  This is rarely the case, though.
