I provided a link to my kernel previously: download from
http://www.lamarowen.net/files/kernel-image-2.4.28_PARI.1lo.SMP.sable_alpha.deb

Install with dpkg.  My /etc/aboot.conf:
alpha2100:~# cat /etc/aboot.conf
0:2/boot/vmlinuz-2.2.20-generic ro root=/dev/sda2
1:2/boot/vmlinuz-2.2.22 ro root=/dev/sda2
3:2/boot/vmlinuz-2.4.28 ro root=/dev/sda2
alpha2100:~#

I boot the kernel with 'boot dka0 -flags 3' and that is the autoboot, for
that matter.  SMP works.  pka is the on-board NCR53C810.  I also have a PCI
DAC960 in there, but haven't yet moved the Debian install to dra0.  I built
the NCR53C810 support monolithic, which means I don't need an initrd to
boot.  I may for the DAC960, though.

I am building a 2.4.29 kernel right now using the Debian kernel-package
build tool 'make-kpkg' which works like this:
you unpack the kernel like normal.  Cd to the kernel tree, do you make
menuconfig (in my case, I used my working 2.4.28 config with make
oldconfig), then you execute 'make-kpkg -rev desired-revision-string' and
let it do all the work.  To get make-kpkg install the kernel-package
package with apt-get install.

My 2.4.29 package will be in the same directory as the 2.4.28 package above
when it is finished.  Good luck.

