When you get this, the two most important questions always are:

* Does the kernel include support for the type of device that holds
  your root filesystem?  (Appropriate SCSI or IDE drivers, software
  RAID if applicable)

* Does the kernel include support for the type of filesystem that.. -''-?

And also

* If either of the above exists as modules, did you build an initrd that
  contains the necessary modules, and was the initrd loaded?


> I know something like this was discussed in a recent  thread and it was 
> suggested that I zero the first few blocks of the disk in case mount was 
> getting confused by what it found there, but I still seem to have the 
> problem.  (Is this specifically an automount problem ?  Can I just turn 
> off automount support ?

Automounting is a way of handling particular types of NFS.  It has
nothing to do with your root file system.

